{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added per-feed `refresh_interval` (minutes, 0 = global interval): new migration adds `feeds.refresh_interval int not null default 0`; field is on the API feed object, accepted by `PUT /v1/feeds/{feedID}` (negative values rejected), stored/read in storage, exposed in the Go client, and editable via a `refresh_interval` number input on the feed edit form. `ScheduleNextCheck` uses the per-feed interval as a strict override when > 0 (it ignores the global scheduler settings and also TTL/Retry-After delays and max-interval caps). Changing the interval to a non-zero value pulls `next_check_at` earlier if needed so it takes effect right away. Two new translation keys were added to all 24 locale files with English text (not translated). Build, unit and integration tests pass; no new tests were added.", "t": 1794463510.966}
{"tool": "_result", "name": "finish", "chars": 55, "t": 1794463510.966}
